  "title": "CHAPTER 2: PHYSICAL GEOGRAPHY OF RAJASTHAN",
  "order": 3,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "txyam5z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Physiographic Divisions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rajasthan can be divided into four main physiographic regions:",
      "id": "d97itay"
    },
    {
      "id": "lt539zf",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "The Thar Desert (North-Western Region)",
        "The Aravalli Range (Central Mountainous Region)",
        "The Eastern Plains (Maidani Pradesh)",
        "The South-Eastern Plateau (Hadoti Plateau)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "je6zmoq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2.1.1 The Thar Desert"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Thar Desert or Great Indian Desert covers approximately 61% of Rajasthan's total area. It includes the districts of Jaisalmer, Barmer, Bikaner, Jodhpur (west), Nagaur, and Pali. The Luni River flows through the southern part of this region. The desert has sand dunes called 'Dhore'. The highest sand dune is found near Sam Sand Dunes in Jaisalmer.",
      "id": "c2mdr5t"
    },
    {
      "id": "u9y77wy",
