    {
      "id": "y6x4k5i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2.1.2 The Aravalli Range"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Aravalli Range is one of the oldest mountain ranges in the world (Pre-Cambrian origin). It divides Rajasthan into western dry region and eastern fertile region. The range extends from Khetri in Jhunjhunu to Palanpur in Gujarat, covering approximately 692 km in Rajasthan.",
      "id": "oa4bfkv"
    },
    {
      "id": "h006tdv",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Detail</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Origin</p>",
            "<p>Pre-Cambrian (World's oldest fold mountain range)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Direction</p>",
            "<p>South-West to North-East</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Total Length (India)</p>",
            "<p>~692 km</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Highest Peak</p>",
            "<p>Guru Shikhar (1722 m) – Mount Abu, Sirohi</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
