      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6gdz306",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2.1.3 Eastern Plains"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The eastern plains region lies between the Aravalli Range and the Chambal River. It comprises the Banas Basin, Banganga Basin, and Gambhir Basin. This region is fertile and densely populated.",
      "id": "59q5ezl"
    },
    {
      "id": "irlwo0i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2.1.4 South-Eastern Plateau (Hadoti Plateau)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This plateau region includes Kota, Bundi, Baran, and Jhalawar. It is made of Vindhyan and Deccan Trap rock formations. The Chambal River and its tributaries drain this region.",
      "id": "lizegjx"
    },
    {
